cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cyRAVEN, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cyRAVEN: Gated Multi-Sample Flow Cytometry Embedding and Differential Analysis"
abstract: >
  An end-to-end workflow for batches of flow cytometry standard (FCS) files.
  Gating thresholds are derived from each sample's own marker density rather than
  transferred from fixed coordinates, populations are scored from a declarative
  specification held in YAML, and one shared UMAP embedding is built per marker
  panel. Differential abundance and differential state are tested on per-sample
  summaries so that donors, not cells, are the replicates. Compositional
  constraints on population percentages are handled with the centred log-ratio,
  batch structure is quantified against a permutation null before any correction
  is applied, and an unsupervised self-organising map clustering provides a
  cross-check that can contradict the gate specification.
authors:
  # CFF requires the ORCID as a full URL, not the bare digits. DESCRIPTION holds
  # the same identifier in the form R expects, which is digits only.
  # `affiliation:` is still unset; add it here if you want it in the citation.
  - given-names: "Bhagesh"
    family-names: "Hunakunti"
    email: "bhunakun@uni-bonn.de"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5957-8005"
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-08-06"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/bhagesh-h/cyRAVEN"
url: "https://bhagesh-h.github.io/cyRAVEN/"
keywords:
  - flow cytometry
  - immunophenotyping
  - gating
  - UMAP
  - differential abundance
  - R
# The methods cyRAVEN implements are due to their original authors. They are not
# duplicated here because a CFF `references:` block requires a complete author
# list per entry, and an incomplete one in a machine-readable file is worse than
# none. inst/CITATION carries them: FlowSOM (Van Gassen et al. 2015), diffcyt
# (Weber et al. 2019), UMAP (McInnes et al. 2018) and LISI (Korsunsky et al.
# 2019). Run citation("cyRAVEN") to see them.
